@flexiarg features/operator-turns-enter-the-observation-vector
@title Read the Operator's Turns, Not His Absence
@style implementation-pattern
@why war-room/wr-16-operationalised-exploit-loops-are-first-class-observation-channels
@holds-at R2
@builds-from problems/operator-turns-become-inference-observations
@audience whoever picks up C-R2
@tone plain-operational
@adjacent-to [futon0/README-inbox-zero.md futon0/holes/excursions/E-inbox-zero-implementation.md]
@references [problems/operator-turns-become-inference-observations
             features/emit-per-tick-mismatch
             war-room/wr-26-a-capability-switched-off-carries-its-re-arm-condition-in-writing-at-the-switch]
@status [status[specified] blocked-by[none]]

! conclusion:
  Add one channel to the mission observation vector that reads a typed
  operator TURN, source it from the mark vocabulary that already types those
  turns, and prove it is read by showing an inference result that moves with
  the channel and not without it.

  + context: The build behind C-R2. The problem statement is
    problems/operator-turns-become-inference-observations and the promotion
    test is p4ng/empirics-futon/promotion-tests.edn. Joe held this card back
    on 2026-08-25 pending "other work on modelling operator turns"; this
    specification is that work, written before any code moves.

    Two halves of the job are in different states, and the pattern's own
    framing ("these are opaque to automation") is now only half true:
      - Turn -> structure EXISTS. futon3c.marks types operator chat-turns
        against a mark vocabulary -- core tier ✘ correction / ✓ approval /
        💡 idea, plus a second-string tier minted from Joe's own clustering-probe
        names -- and keeps agent self-talk out of the gold channel by
        construction (author-invariance). Marks are queryable as evidence tags
        precisely because the text index strips the glyphs, and the evidence
        bodies are searchable through the futon1b fts5 sidecar.
      - Structure -> inference DOES NOT. futon3c.aif.observe/channel-keys is
        ten channels wide and every one of them is a function of mission state.
        Nothing in that vector is a function of anything Joe did.
    So this is not "build a turn parser". It is "connect two things that were
    built years apart and never wired to each other".

  + adjacent: Most of that wire is built already, in a project that was not
    aiming at R2. futon0/README-inbox-zero and E-inbox-zero-implementation
    (slices 1-11, merged 2026-08-21..24) supply, and are RUNNING on zone as of
    2026-08-25 18:27:
      - a turn-level producer with an explicit witness. dev.clj's
        record-inbox-zero-tool-results! mints a session-file claim only from a
        tool_result that is not an error -- intent is not authorship -- carrying
        {:seat/id "seat:<agent>:<session>", :witness/type :tool-edit,
        :witness/id "toolu_..."}. 54 claims on disk, 3,621 file observations,
        115 commit observations. A turn, typed, durable, keyed to the act.
      - basis-typed edges. futon3.inbox-zero.infer ranks evidence
        :direct / :corroborated / :weak, fails closed, and gates :weak behind an
        explicit flag. This channel needs exactly that: a value carrying how it
        was come by, the way :selection-source does.
      - CONFIRMATION MINTS; INFERENCE ONLY PROPOSES. The confirmation keystroke
        converts inference-strength into witness-strength. That is the
        :acknowledged? producer generalised -- an operator act that changes the
        epistemic status of a record -- and it is the smallest complete instance
        of what this feature claims. The cost of skipping it is measured:
        autoclock mission-linkage, inferred and written without confirmation,
        "present on 65% of turns and substantially wrong" (M-futon-problems D8).
      - a delivery lane with an acknowledgement lifecycle. The slice-4 followup
        queue is exact-seat, deduped and busy-gated, and carries
        :queued/:delivered/:acked/:cancelled/:expired with timestamps. An
        acknowledgement is already a durable record there. The operator lane has
        no such record anywhere.
      - the same ladder one level up. README-inbox-zero's escalation tiers
        (0 nobody / 1 responsible seat / 2 sweeper / 3 Joe) are silent/brief/nag
        under other names, and its rule -- "volume is never by itself a tier-3
        signal" -- is what the nag gate is trying to say.

    And it currently fails the same way, which is the sharpest reason to build
    on it rather than beside it: over 30 hours its tier 1 fired zero times.
    See FAILURE-MODES.

  + joined: What the 2026-08-25 session established, by reading the running
    system rather than the pattern. Five edges exist and nothing joins them;
    the join key is the session id, the same string in all of them.

      turn -> pattern   context-retrieval evidence (dev.clj context-retrieval!)
                        per turn, (agent-id, session-id, turn-n) -> ranked
                        pattern ids with cosine scores. RUNNING, including on
                        operator turns: the live ring buffer holds queries
                        beginning "Surface: emacs-repl / From: joe".
      turn -> file      :inbox-zero/session-file-claim, :witness/id = tool-use id
      turn -> commit    :inbox-zero/session-commit-link, :basis typed
      turn -> mission   the seat clock, stamped as a `Mission:` commit trailer
      pattern -> mission  the library's @why links (static)

    The structure those nodes want is a CASCADE, and the consumer already
    exists: futon3c.peripheral.strategic-cascade builds a reason-bearing
    frontier over {:shown [ids] :semilattice {:descent [[a b]]} :policy-holes}
    and live-wm-selection consumes it. Its edge schema already carries
    :status #{:proposed :witnessed :challenged :retracted} and refuses an edge
    without provenance, for the stated reason that "an embedding suggestion can
    never become an unattributed graph fact" (futon2 mission_control_graph).
    So the promotion economy of cascades/edges-earn-permanence is in code, not
    only in the library.

    One namespace gap, measured: valid-control-pattern-id? requires a `p4ng/`
    prefix; 58 of the 1400 rows in futon3/resources/sigils/patterns-index.tsv
    are p4ng/*, and per-turn retrieval returns shelf ids like
    devmap-coherence/*, fulab/*, iching/*. The consumer cannot currently eat
    what the producer makes. That bridge is the smallest thing standing between
    this feature and a live consumer.

  + IF:
    Operator turns are captured, typed, and text-searchable.

  + HOWEVER:
    The observation vector cannot see them, and the one place the apparatus
    does claim to represent Joe is unwired.

    `operator-lane/nag?` is a conjunction of four terms and the fourth is
    `:acknowledged?`. Nothing sets it. `operator-lane-adapter` assembles nine
    descriptive keys onto every item and that is not among them;
    `operator-bulletin/newly-acknowledged` computes the acknowledged set as a
    pure function and has no caller outside its own test, its docstring
    deferring persistence to "the forward-model adapter" that does not do it;
    the one path that bypasses the classifier with a pre-set lane reads
    `data/wm/needs-you.edn`, which is `[]`. So nag 0 of 111 on the live
    bulletin is not a threshold that wants tuning. The gate cannot open,
    because the term that would open it has no producer -- and that term is
    definitionally an operator turn: it means Joe LOOKED.

  + THEN:
    Three steps, and only the third one closes the ring. Keep them separately
    reviewable, because the first is cheap and reads like progress.

    0. Wire acknowledgement. Persist `newly-acknowledged` at bulletin pull and
       feed `:acknowledged?` back through the adapter. This makes nag reachable
       and is worth doing -- but it is a repair to a dangling seam, NOT this
       feature. Report it as such. (See FAILURE-MODES: it is separately
       sufficient to satisfy the promotion test as first drafted, which is a
       defect in that test rather than a licence to claim the ring.)
    1. Emit an operator-turn observation. One channel appended to
       `channel-keys`, normalised to [0,1] like its neighbours, whose value is
       a function of the marks on turns addressed to the item -- the obvious
       first cut being recent-correction-or-approval pressure, so that ✘ and ✓
       are distinguishable and neither is confused with silence. State its
       provenance the way `:selection-source` distinguishes an operator pick
       from the selector's -- and prefer inbox-zero's three-class basis ranking
       (:direct / :corroborated / :weak) to inventing a second vocabulary for
       the same distinction.
       The cheapest honest version reuses the followup queue rather than the
       mark corpus: an :acked followup IS an operator turn -- durable,
       exact-seat, already timestamped. Building the channel on acknowledgement
       first gets a real operator act into the vector on rails that exist; the
       mark corpus is the richer second source, not a prerequisite.
    2. Show it is read. Run one window of >= 111 classifications with the
       channel live, and the same window with it held at a constant, and record
       both inference results.

  + BECAUSE:
    WR-16 rules that an operationalised loop the operator actually runs is a
    first-class observation channel, and the mark vocabulary is that loop: Joe
    already types his own turns, in a vocabulary he partly named. What the
    apparatus does with them today is measure how long it has been since he
    appeared. The per-class credit collapse to 0.009 is what a missing variable
    looks like from inside the model -- "he considered this and declined" and
    "he was elsewhere" arrive at the estimator as the same event, so the
    estimator learns that the operator is noise.

  + FAILURE-MODES:
    - The acknowledgement fix wearing the ring's clothes. Step 0 alone makes
      nag fire, which satisfies the promotion test's STATEMENT while no
      operator turn has entered the observation vector at all. The null control
      catches it (disable the turn channel, nag still fires, so the channel is
      not what moved it) -- but a statement that a different repair can satisfy
      is a weak statement, and the test should be tightened before it is run,
      not after it passes.
    - Reading the operator's presence again in a new shape. A channel whose
      value rises with turn COUNT is days-since-last-activity with the sign
      flipped. The channel has to separate turn TYPES or it has added nothing.
    - Grading ourselves on our own transcript. R9 and WR-0: run against our own
      history this measures our observation channel on data our observation
      channel produced. The external fixture in promotion-tests.edn (SWE-bench,
      dated, outcome known) is what makes the verdict issuable.
    - Reading a stale index and calling it a quiet operator. The sidecar keeps
      two watermarks and `ev_fts` / `ev_attr` can disagree; futon1b/README-fts.md
      §"can disagree -- check both" is explicit that a body missing from one is
      not evidence of a missing turn. Check both before concluding zero.
    - Running under an unrecorded switch state. `FUTON3C_MARK_RECOGNIZER=false`
      and `FUTON3C_SELF_MARKS=false` each silence part of the input. WR-26: the
      pilot records which switches were in which state, or its zero means
      nothing.
    - Inheriting a ladder whose top rung has no producer. Verified on zone,
      2026-08-25: storage/inbox-zero/escalation-ledger.edn holds 3,263
      promotion plans from 08-24T12:11 to 08-25T17:55, ALL :verdict :held,
      :held/reason :nothing-promotable, :route/tier 2, recipient
      "street-sweeper". :include is empty in all 3,263; the 37,195 path
      exclusions are 35,714 :unattributed and 1,481 :other-seat. The cause is
      upstream of attribution and is an identity join, not a threshold: dev.clj
      calls `turn-promotion/launch-at-turn-end!` with the invoke path's session
      id, which is sometimes nil, and `promote-at-turn-end!` builds
      `(str "seat:" agent-id ":" session-id)` with no guard -- so a plan's seat
      reads `seat:f35-guide:` while every claim that same agent minted reads
      `seat:f35-guide:83f524b5-...`. promotion.clj includes a path only when
      `(= seat-id (:seat/id (first claims)))`, so a sessionless plan can never
      include anything. All six seats in the ledger are sessionless. Every step
      is fail-closed and correct, and the system produces nothing. A channel
      built on this substrate inherits that: check the seat ids join before
      reading any zero as an operator being quiet.
    - Laundering. `:acknowledged?` and the mark channel are DESCRIPTIVE. INV-5
      forbids a predicted-importance signal reaching the lane classifier, and a
      channel derived from Joe's turns is exactly the thing someone will be
      tempted to feed back in as predicted importance.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Name the channel and its normalisation -- one entry appended to
         channel-keys, with the [0,1] meaning stated in the docstring the way
         the other ten state theirs.]
    next[Decide what the null control HOLDS the channel at, and why that value:
         a constant chosen to make the difference show is not a control.]
    next[Pick the >= 111-item window and record it before running, so the live
         and frozen runs are the same window.]
    next[Tighten the R2 promotion test so step 0 alone cannot satisfy it.]
    next[Decide the source: acknowledged followups (rails exist, thin signal)
         or the mark corpus (rich, needs the fts join). Not exclusive, and the
         first is much cheaper.]
    next[Before either, make the seat-id join hold -- a sessionless seat id is
         being produced at turn end today and joins to nothing.]
    next[Measure top-3 embedding retrieval precision before building on it. A
         sampled turn returned iching/hexagram-39-jian at rank 2 (0.4744)
         against rank 1's 0.4809; nothing in the stack knows whether that is a
         hit. A cascade inherits every error in its nodes and compounds them
         into edges, and an operator-facing cascade spends the one resource
         this design is short of.]
    next[Bridge the 58 p4ng/* control patterns to shelf retrieval, or state
         that the WM consumer is out of scope for the first cut.]
